                <pb facs="0509" n="1243" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1243"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-14"><hi rendition="#italic">April 14,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>More security for life is felt by missionaries in Asia Minor. Their letters show
                    that my demand on the Porte to send telegraphic orders everywhere for their
                    protection was complied with. Turkish Government expresses determination to
                    preserve social order.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
